---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import career from '../data/career.json';
import places from '../data/places.json';
---

<Base
  title="About Acquah Yeboah | yeboah.works"
  description="Acquah Yeboah, also writing as Acquah Nana Yeboah. Nigerian researcher, writer and builder working on governance and African tech, based in Rabat, Morocco."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">About</p>
      <h1 class="page-header__title reveal reveal--delay-1">Acquah Nana Yeboah</h1>
      <p class="page-header__subtitle reveal reveal--delay-2">
        Researcher, writer, and builder from southern Nigeria. Currently in Rabat, Morocco.
      </p>
      <a href="/docs/acquah-yeboah-cv.pdf" download class="btn reveal reveal--delay-3" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        Download CV <span aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="bio">
    <div class="bio__inner">
      <div class="bio__text reveal">
        <p>I'm Acquah Yeboah. I write and publish as Acquah Nana Yeboah, and most people just call me Yeboah.</p>
        <p>I grew up between Bayelsa and Delta States in South-South Nigeria. Growing up in the Niger Delta made me interested in the relationship between public resources, governance and development, particularly why communities with considerable natural wealth often struggle to access basic public services.</p>
        <p>My journey into civic leadership began during Nigeria's national youth service in 2018. I coordinated a team of over 30 corps members, led voter education campaigns reaching an estimated 5,000 citizens and established civic education clubs in two secondary schools. I later continued this work through peacebuilding research, electoral advocacy and public accountability initiatives.</p>
        <p>Journalism introduced me to another dimension of development: technology and entrepreneurship. At Techloy and TheOuut, I covered more than a thousand stories about startups, investment and innovation across emerging markets. I subsequently moved into corporate communications, helping institutions communicate more effectively with employees, customers and other stakeholders.</p>
        <p>In 2024, I moved to Morocco on a full scholarship to study Collective Intelligence at Mohammed VI Polytechnic University. My research and student leadership experiences there broadened my understanding of Africa and strengthened my interest in how people, organisations and technology can work together to solve complex problems.</p>
        <p>Today, I serve as Head of Communications and Public Relations at the Centre for Advancement of Governance and Democracy (CAGAD), where I am also a founding member. I co-founded LogaLab, a civic technology initiative making public finance information more accessible, and contribute to fiscal accountability research as a BudgIT fellow.</p>
        <p>Much of my work revolves around a central question: how can we build institutions that make better decisions with people, rather than simply for them?</p>
        <p>Outside work, I enjoy reading, music, writing and building digital products. This website is where I document that journey.</p>
        <a href="/impact" class="section-link">Leadership and impact <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="bio__photo reveal reveal--delay-2">
        <img src="/img/Acquah-headshot.jpeg" alt="Acquah Yeboah" width="400" height="533" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="beliefs">
    <div class="beliefs__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">What I believe</p>
      <blockquote class="beliefs__quote reveal reveal--delay-1">
        Democracy should be more than an election every four years. Citizens should have access to public information, meaningful opportunities to shape decisions and the ability to hold institutions accountable. Technology can help, but lasting change also requires trust, capable institutions and a culture of participation.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="places">
    <div class="places__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">Places that shaped me</p>
      <div class="places__scroll reveal reveal--delay-1">
        {places.map((place) => (
          <div class="place-card">
            <p class="place-card__name">{place.name}</p>
            {place.date && <p class="place-card__date">{place.date}</p>}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="career">
    <div class="career__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">My path</p>
      <h2 class="reveal reveal--delay-1">Career</h2>
      <div class="career__timeline reveal reveal--delay-2">
        {career.map((job) => (
          <div class="career-item">
            <div class="career-item__logo">
              {job.logo
                ? <img src={job.logo} alt={job.org} />
                : <span class="career-item__logo-placeholder">{job.org.charAt(0)}</span>}
            </div>
            <div class="career-item__content">
              <p class="career-item__years">{job.years}</p>
              <p class="career-item__role">{job.role}</p>
              <p class="career-item__org">{job.org}</p>
              <span class={`career-item__type career-item__type--${job.type}`}>{job.type}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="right-now">
    <div class="right-now__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">Right now</p>
      <h2 class="reveal reveal--delay-1">What I'm working on</h2>
      <div class="reveal reveal--delay-2" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p><strong>CAGAD:</strong> Leading communications and advocacy for Manifesto Watch 2027 and strengthening institutional communications.</p>
        <p><strong>LogaLab:</strong> Developing a private-beta civic technology platform, starting with fiscal data for Bayelsa's eight local government areas.</p>
        <p><strong>BudgIT:</strong> Reviewing quarterly budget implementation and fiscal transparency, with primary responsibility for Bayelsa.</p>
        <p><strong>Company Scout:</strong> Building an evidence-led company research and outreach tool.</p>
        <p>I'm open to research, communications, writing and policy collaborations.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="section-link">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
